From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: arm64: dts: sun50i-h5-nanopi-r1s-h5: add #address-cells/#size-cells to ehci1

The on-board RTL8153 is described as a child of ehci1 with reg = <1>
(its USB port number), but ehci1 inherits no #address-cells/#size-cells
from sunxi-h3-h5.dtsi. dtc falls back to the defaults of 2 and 1 and
warns:

  Warning (reg_format): /soc/usb@1c1b000/device@1:reg: property has
  invalid length (4 bytes) (#address-cells == 2, #size-cells == 1)
  Warning (avoid_default_addr_size): /soc/usb@1c1b000/device@1:
  Relying on default #address-cells value

Use the cells that usb-hcd.yaml / usb-device.yaml require for a USB
hub port: #address-cells = <1>, #size-cells = <0>.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h5-nanopi-r1s-h5.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h5-nanopi-r1s-h5.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h5-nanopi-r1s-h5.dts
index 10dff5c..2fa1c19 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h5-nanopi-r1s-h5.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h5-nanopi-r1s-h5.dts
@@ -116,6 +116,8 @@
 };
 
 &ehci1 {
+	#address-cells = <1>;
+	#size-cells = <0>;
 	status = "okay";
 
 	rtl8153: device@1 {
-- 
Armbian

